[2026-10-11T16:53:05Z + 232.1s] QUESTION The brief does not say what to do or how to close when `transfer_to_agent`, `schedule_callback` or `add_note` itself fails (ok false or 500).
[2026-10-11T16:53:05Z + 232.1s] QUESTION Brief A rule 37 says to close as `no_promise` / `service_error` after a second failure; with Brief B, when another product has an earlier non-paid note (for example refused), the closing reason is that note's reason by "the reason of the first product, in `get_account` order, whose note is not `paid`". A promise_failed fallback is kept last only for the case where no note exists.
[2026-10-11T16:53:05Z + 232.1s] QUESTION Rule 42 uses queue `general` with closing reason `human`; the queue value and the reason differ and are mapped as the brief states.
